dium", "notes": ["Incumbent Bill Huizenga (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 4th District pairs a Republican-tilting electorate with a long-serving incumbent, Bill Huizenga, against state senator Sean McCann, a well-funded challenger backed by surrogates including Governor Whitmer and Senator Slotkin. Outside groups have poured roughly $3.3 million into attacks on Huizenga, while McCann has raised nearly as much as the incumbent himself. A Green Party candidate appears on the ballot but is not a factor.\n\nThe evidence points to a genuine tossup with a slight Democratic edge. Five of ten expert raters now call the race a Lean D flip, while the rest call it a Tossup, and two prediction markets put McCann's odds near 60 percent. Polling is sparse and contradictory: the most recent survey gives Huizenga a three-point lead, but earlier polls, mostly Democratic-sponsored, showed McCann narrowly ahead. The race sits at the margin of the Lean D and Tossup categories, with meaningful uncertainty in both directions.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5309, "margin": 0.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4667, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4711, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4732, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4842, "margin": 0.3}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4178, "margin": -0.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4942, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4707, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.417, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4657, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5306, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4314, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.5595, "margin": 0.4}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4501, "margin": -0.3}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.5027, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4045, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4996, "margin